  Temperatures = 296 400 500 600 700 800 1000 1200 K                71 1451
                                                                    71 1451
 THEORY                                                             71 1451
 ------                                                             71 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics    71 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. The          71 1451
 inelastic scattering thermal scattering law data for uranium       71 1451
 mononitride (UN) was developed using ab initio lattice dynamics    71 1451
 methods [1-2]. The Full Law Analysis Scattering System Hub         71 1451
 (FLASSH) code was used to produce MF=7 and MT=2 and 4 for N in     71 1451
 UN (U natural enrichment) [3]. The incoherent scattering cross     71 1451
 section is stored in MT=2 for N in UN along with half of the UN    71 1451
 compound's coherent elastic cross section.                         71 1451
                                                                    71 1451
 The UN evaluation was improved over the ENDF/B-VIII.0              71 1451
 evaluation with key updates: (1) lattice constants from            71 1451
 experimental values were used [2] and (2) the coherent elastic     71 1451
 (MT2) contribution was updated to the cubic evaluation in          71 1451
 FLASSH [3].                                                        71 1451
